        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "Materials and methods",
          "quote": "To validate the effectiveness of the pulsed-wave laser for alloying refractory elements, a third print batch was performed by blending pure CrCoNi powder with different amounts of pure W powder (3 wt% and 10 wt%) with similar particle sizes of 20–45 lm. The maximum amount of blended W powder was set as 10 wt% to avoid the formation of a detrimental secondary phase [19]. The in-situ alloyed (CrCoNi)100-xWx alloy samples were printed using parameters selected from the optimized process window for printing pure CrCoNi alloy.",
